<article class="env-definition" id="02OT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02OT">Definition <span data-tag="02OT">31.24.4</span>.</a> Let $f : (X, \mathcal{O}_ X) \to (Y, \mathcal{O}_ Y)$ be a morphism of locally ringed spaces. We say that <em>pullbacks of meromorphic functions are defined for $f$</em> if for every pair of open $U \subset X$, $V \subset Y$ such that $f(U) \subset V$, and any section $s \in \Gamma (V, \mathcal{S}_ Y)$ the pullback $f^\sharp (s) \in \Gamma (U, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ is an element of $\Gamma (U, \mathcal{S}_ X)$. </p>
</article>